# Triumph 2000 Mk2 four-door saloon, 1969-1977.
#
# The 1969 facelift of the 2000: longer at both ends, with a full-width nose and
# grille, larger headlamps in a wider surround, a longer boot and HORIZONTAL rear
# lamp clusters. The pre-facelift Mk2 (1969-1974) is modelled; the 1974 facelift's
# revised grille and trim, and the 2000 TC, are not.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triumph_2000
# https://triumph2000register.co.uk/the-cars/technical-specifications/
#
# Dimensions 4.630 x 1.690 x 1.420 m, wheelbase 2.690 m, pre-facelift Mk2, from
# the Triumph 2000 Register specifications, which give 4.66 x 1.71 x 1.44 m after
# the 1974 facelift. Mirrors take the modelled width to 1.980 m.
#
# Colours are Triumph's own paint names, drawn from the Register's list of genuine
# Triumph finishes: Saffron, Pimento, French Blue and Emerald, all of them offered
# on the 2000/2500 in the Mk2 years. **The Register does not allocate each colour
# to a mark and year**, so the individual intro and retire months here are the
# road-presence dates of the objects, not evidence that the colour began on that
# month. Weights saffron 3, emerald 3, pimento 2, frenchblue 2, total 10,
# provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 160 km/h for the 2000 and 2000 TC. Comfort 85/458, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 85, a step above the Mk1's 85-minute figure at the same value
# because the Mk2 rides and insulates better. Classes 1,2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence: October 1969 intro, retires staggered 1986-1989 on a
# twelve- to twenty-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/triumph-2000-mk2.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/triumph-2000-mk2.dae (58 objects). References:
# citycars/references/triumph-2000-mk2/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons; image 1 is
# an oblique view, so the flank is dimension-calibrated).
#
# This master is the basis of the 2500, which shares the shell.
#
# Accepted deviations: the model is more faceted than the photographs,
# particularly the shoulders and roof corners. At 128 px the full-width nose, the
# separate boot and the horizontal rear lamps read as the Mk2.

obj=citycar
name=Triumph2000Mk2(Saffron)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1969
intro_month=10
retire_year=1989
retire_month=6
speed=160
class=1,2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=85
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=458

